callback sees the tracked work's name. <code>None</code> reads the real driver status; <code>Some Pending</code> retains the buffer until a later observation; <code>Some (Error error)</code> substitutes status <code>Error</code> and its optional error text. Install before submission with <code>Pending</code>, then switch to <code>Error</code> at the explicit wait, so post-launch bookkeeping cannot reap the buffer first. Only finite, normally submitted work is needed. The runner's resulting failure stays latched after this scope ends. Restores the prior callback on return or exception; does not alter Metal's actual command buffers.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-status_for_reap\"><a href=\"#val-status_for_reap\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> status_for_reap : <span><span class=\"label\">what</span>:string <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><a href=\"#type-status\">status</a> option</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Backend-side read of the test seam; <code>None</code> outside a test scope.</p></div></div>"}